  "body": "stacked on #3059\n\n## What changed\n\n- In `chamfer_open_runs` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/chamfer.rs`), mapped the error when an open edge chain collapses to fewer than two points to return `\"a chamfer edge collapses to one point - re-pick the edge\"` instead of bubbling up the generic `\"a centerline run needs at least two points\"` message.\n- Documented the defensive guard that verifies `pass` has at least two points.\n- Extracted open chamfer refusal tests into `crates/motion/tests/chamfer_open_refusals.rs`, keeping `chamfer_circular.rs` under the 400-line limit.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test chamfer_open_refusals`: 3 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test chamfer_circular`: 10 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test chamfer_open_edges`: 5 passed.\n- `coderabbit review --agent --base-commit 2fbe6f2fb`: passed with 0 findings.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `an_open_chamfer_collapsing_to_one_point_refuses_by_name`\n- `an_open_chamfer_with_a_collapsed_segment_refuses_by_name`\n- `an_open_chamfer_without_a_model_wall_refuses_by_name`\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Heavy gate suite was not run locally.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #3086\n",
